WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.660
When it comes to thrilling theatrical experiences,
there's nothing quite like a good action movie.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.010
Between fast pacing, epic moments of suspense,
deep-seated drama between the heroes and villains,

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.220
and, of course, tons of stunts, the genre
has a lot to offer audiences.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.890
Here are some of the high octane movies you'll
definitely want to sit through before it's

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:20.750
all said and done to get your cinematic adrenaline
rush.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:21.950
Face/Off

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.630
This film has such a preposterous concept
that would have been a ridiculous misfire

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:30.100
had it been made by anybody but legendary
Hong Kong auteur John Woo, director of classics

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.110
like Hard Boiled and The Killer.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.140
But Face/Off might just be his best.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:38.940
The film also finds the perfect role for Nicolas
Cage as Castor Troy, a giddy, crazed terrorist

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.740
who tries to kill FBI agent Sean Archer, portrayed
by John Travolta.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:47.340
In order to learn where Castor hid a massive
bomb, Archer has his own face surgically replaced

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:52.090
with Castor's…and then Castor gets his replaced
with Archer's, which is an absolutely terrible

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.090
idea.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:57.670
"It's like looking in a mirror, only not."

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:01.890
Add in a few plane chases and some epic shootout
sequences, and you've got yourself a wild

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.890
ride at the movies.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:04.960
The Raid

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.689
Gareth Evans' The Raid is a claustrophobic
police thriller that hits the ground running

00:01:08.689 --> 00:01:09.689
almost immediately.

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:13.970
A young police officer named Rama heads off
to join his armed-to-the-teeth S.W.A.T. team

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.640
taking down a run-down Jakarta apartment building.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.522
The goal is to eliminate a crime lord and
his top associates who run the block and allow

00:01:20.522 --> 00:01:21.939
criminals sanctuary.

00:01:21.939 --> 00:01:24.110
The movie plays out like a real-life video
game.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:28.080
The elite police squad clears the lower floors
and handles various thugs until they realize

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.829
they've been trapped and are being hunted
by a gaggle of ticked-off criminals.

00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:36.049
This changes everything for Rama and his squad,
as they'll now have to fight their way out

00:01:36.049 --> 00:01:39.340
of the situation and hope to walk away with
their lives.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:41.170
Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon

00:01:41.170 --> 00:01:45.770
Imagine a sweeping war drama and epic romance
like Gone With the Wind…but everybody in

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.730
it has supernatural martial arts fighting
abilities, and the way they fight is more

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.610
technically perfect and beautiful than the
greatest ballet company.

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:56.590
That may sound ridiculous, but in the able
hands of director Ang Lee and cast members

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:01.420
Chow Yun-fat, Michelle Yeoh , Zhang Ziyi and
Chang Chen, the result is one of the most

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.149
stunningly beautiful and deeply moving films
ever made.

00:02:04.149 --> 00:02:08.340
There are also many iconic martial arts sequences
in the film, such as the near wordless battle

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.670
in the sky, on the fragile tips of trees.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:14.370
While action movies often rely on special
effects to do all of the heavy lifting, in

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:18.650
Crouching Tiger, they merely enhance or flavor
the actors' abilities already captured on

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:19.650
film.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:20.650
John Wick

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:25.140
Ultra-violent revenge movies generally don't
have plots hinging on an adorable puppy, but

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.950
that's part of what makes John Wick so delightfully
different.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:31.709
After the loss of his wife, the title assassin,
played by Keanu Reeves, tries to fill the

00:02:31.709 --> 00:02:36.260
void in his life by adopting a cute dog named
Daisy and riding around in his classic Ford

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.260
Mustang.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.550
After he refuses to sell it to a Russian gangster,
the spurned buyer and his cronies follow Wick

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:46.600
home, knock him out, steal the car, and even
take out their payback on the poor dog.

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:51.140
Exacting his revenge pulls Wick back into
the seedy underbelly of organized crime.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:57.140
"People keep asking if I'm back and I haven't
really had an answer.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:03:00.000
But now yeah, I'm thinking I'm back!"

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.650
And that spawns numerous atmospheric gun battles
and fistfights across nightclubs, churches,

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.900
safe houses, docks, and more.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.810
This is exactly the kind of action movie that's
perfect for watching with friends, rewinding

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:15.290
and replaying favorite moments because they're
just too good to be believed.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.290
Baby Driver

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:20.310
Edgar Wright is best known for directing Shaun
of the Dead, Hot Fuzz, and Scott Pilgrim vs.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:23.980
the World, and those are all predominantly
comedies laced with some innovative action

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:24.980
sequences.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:28.659
With Baby Driver, however, he makes the leap
to full-blown action fare, and the result

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:31.459
is as frenetic and assured as Baby's driving.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:35.180
Ansel Elgort plays the title character, a
young but very skilled driver recruited to

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.290
handle the getaway car for a heist squad.

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:41.050
The unreal stunts in Baby Driver make the
movie deliriously fun, and the filmmaker's

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:46.349
extensive movie knowledge and vocabulary make
for a mishmash of satisfying homages and techniques

00:03:46.349 --> 00:03:47.659
gleaned from other films.

00:03:47.659 --> 00:03:52.030
The end result is pretty much everything audiences
could want out of an action film.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:53.049
Rogue One

00:03:53.049 --> 00:03:57.260
It would be both sacrilegious and inaccurate
to say that Rogue One is the best Star Wars

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.260
movie.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.470
It's not even part of the main storyline—it's
a side story about a scrappy crew that comes

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.450
together to steal the Death Star's plans and
find its weakness.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:09.100
Therein lies the reason why Rogue One is great—it's
less a space opera or sci-fi movie and more

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.959
a heist movie that just happens to be set
in the Star Wars universe.

00:04:11.959 --> 00:04:15.970
As the team comes together, plans the crime,
and pulls it off -- although not without severe

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:20.350
consequences -- the action is as unrelenting
as it is eye-popping.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:21.500
Edge of Tomorrow

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.200
A cross between Groundhog Day and Independence
Day might not work for everyone, but director

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.370
Doug Liman crafted Edge of Tomorrow into one
of the most innovative action-adventure movies

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.370
in years.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:34.350
In this smart and chaotic sci-fi/military
adventure, seemingly indestructible aliens

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:38.940
called Mimics terrorize Earth until they have
to square off against Tom Cruise's Major William

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:39.940
Craig.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:43.090
They take him out too— but Craig gets caught
in a time loop and keeps returning to the

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:47.930
moment just before his demise to fight and
fail again and again until he can figure out

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.110
a way to defeat them.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:52.740
Edge of Tomorrow is a video game-inspired
action movie with something of a moral lesson:

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:57.540
If at first you don't succeed at destroying
aliens, try, try again.

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:58.880
Guardians of the Galaxy

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:02.810
Sometimes the problem with comic book movies
is that they take themselves way too seriously

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:06.330
and forget the whole point of their source
material—they're supposed to be fun, and

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.400
also a little ridiculous.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:12.330
But Guardians of the Galaxy embraces its own
DNA to deliver one of the most purely enjoyable

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.419
comic book-based movies of all time.

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:18.960
It's as much a comedy as it is an outer-space
action ride, with Chris Pratt perfectly cast

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.220
as the funny and fearless Peter Quill, the
so-called "Star-Lord."

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:27.199
Add in a space prison, a telepathic arrow,
some sublime '70s rock classics, a foul-mouthed

00:05:27.199 --> 00:05:32.419
raccoon, a talking tree, and one epic space
battle, and the end result is a joyous blast.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:34.440
"And bring it down hard!"

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.900
"What are you doing?"

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.639
"Dance-off, bro!

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:42.250
Me and you!"

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.250
District 13

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:47.580
In the early 2000s, parkour, the sport of
ignoring the laws of physics to walk up walls

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.690
and jump from one thing to another, was a
minor fad in the United States.

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.590
In Europe, the practice is a way of life.

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:57.270
The craze gave the world at least one great
parkour-themed movie: District 13.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:01.069
The title is a nod to the poverty-ridden and
overcrowded Paris suburb where the film takes

00:06:01.069 --> 00:06:05.039
place, and the film is set in the not-too-distant
future wherein the government keeps the area

00:06:05.039 --> 00:06:08.669
in check by surrounding it with high walls
topped with razor wire.

00:06:08.669 --> 00:06:11.960
Gangs control the lawless prison colony and
make their living running drugs.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:16.319
A man -- played by David Belle, a creator
of parkour -- tries to fight the gangs, which

00:06:16.319 --> 00:06:21.830
he does with his wits as well as his gravity-defying
parkour skills, executed without wires or

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:22.830
CGI.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.319
Ong Bak: The Thai Warrior

00:06:25.319 --> 00:06:28.770
This low-budget martial arts adventure from
Thailand more than makes up for its simple

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.090
plot and straightforward presentation with
the sheer force of its unbelievable star,

00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:34.090
Tony Jaa.

00:06:34.090 --> 00:06:37.630
In the film, a rural village is distraught
after thugs from Bangkok steal the head of

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.710
the town's cherished Buddha statue.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:44.000
Jaa plays Ting, the brave local who ventures
into the city to retrieve the head, with only

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.410
his Muay Thai fighting skills to protect himself.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:50.440
Fortunately, Jaa is one of the most agile
and adept martial artists in the world, which

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:53.680
he proves during some brutal underground fights.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.960
Rumble in the Bronx

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:58.860
After decades of comedy-laced action films
made him a massive star around the world,

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:03.100
English-speaking audiences were finally introduced
to the singular cinema of Jackie Chan with

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:06.849
Rumble in the Bronx, and it was very representative
of Chan's talents.

00:07:06.849 --> 00:07:10.830
The simple plot is about good guys versus
bad guys involved in illegal diamond deals,

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:16.020
but there's also a romance, Chan's self-deprecating
humor, and, of course, stunts that look impossible

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:18.860
but aren't because Jackie Chan never fakes
it.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:20.009
Casino Royale

00:07:20.009 --> 00:07:24.599
By the time Pierce Brosnan's tenure as 007
was done, the James Bond franchise had descended

00:07:24.599 --> 00:07:29.220
into a checklist of the familiar: tuxedos,
gadgets, shaken-not-stirred martinis, and,

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.949
of course, all the Bond girls.

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:34.880
So, when Daniel Craig suited up for the super
spy, it was time for a modern twist on the

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:37.720
formula, and Casino Royale knocked it out
of the park.

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:41.860
Craig took over as a younger version of James
Bond, and the movie took cues from other forward-thinking

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:42.990
action films.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:47.520
It's gritty, intense, and completely lacking
the usual James Bond smirkiness, delivering

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:51.610
the best entry in the series since Sean Connery
was creating action movie tropes back in the

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:52.720
'60s.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:53.720
Ip Man

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:58.729
Action movies are usually over-the-top, absurdly
fun cinematic roller coasters, but every now

00:07:58.729 --> 00:08:00.970
and then, one of them is actually a true story.

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:05.639
Ip Man is the loosely biographical story of
a Wing Chun grandmaster who famously trained

00:08:05.639 --> 00:08:09.110
the all-time greatest martial arts film star,
Bruce Lee.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:13.009
In Ip Man, the title character is the best
martial artist and fighting trainer in the

00:08:13.009 --> 00:08:14.580
Chinese city of Foshan.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.580
His low-key life and appreciation of martial
arts are tested after the Japanese invasion

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:19.580
of 1937.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:24.720
He competes for bags of rice in fighting competitions
against Japanese troops, and he seeks revenge

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:27.490
when his friend Lin disappears for good after
a bout.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:31.509
At the heart of the movie, however, are the
high-stakes battles between Chinese and Japanese

00:08:31.509 --> 00:08:34.410
fighters, all under the backdrop of war.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:35.410
Dredd

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:40.051
The 1995 version of Judge Dredd was merely
an action vehicle for Sylvester Stallone in

00:08:40.051 --> 00:08:42.360
the waning years of his tenure as an action
star.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:47.060
As such, it was an endlessly violent shoot-'em-up
that lacked the humor, irony, and satire of

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.410
its source comics.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.640
"I. Am.

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:50.640
The.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:51.640
LAW."

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.200
But Dredd is the rare case of Hollywood getting
a remake right.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:58.500
The exceptionally violent but cheeky action
extravaganza features Karl Urban as the title

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.500
character.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:03.520
And this time, Dredd is the most fearsome
of the judge-jury-executioners that stalk

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.390
around the futuristic, radiation-soaked wasteland
that is Mega City.

00:09:07.390 --> 00:09:11.240
Dredd maims his way through his days as he
tries to eradicate a new drug that's threatening

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.740
the innocents around town.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:16.149
"I advise you to hold your breath."

00:09:16.149 --> 00:09:17.149
Kung Fu Hustle

00:09:17.149 --> 00:09:20.980
What if they made a movie that played like
a hilarious, live-action cartoon, but it also

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:24.580
had non-stop kicking, punching, and intricately
choreographed fight scenes?

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:27.920
Well, that would be an irresistible movie
called Kung Fu Hustle.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:33.209
Chinese superstar Stephen Chow directs, co-writes,
and stars in this dazzling and dizzying action

00:09:33.209 --> 00:09:35.690
epic set in China in the 1940s.

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:40.190
Chow plays a guy named Sing who's desperate
to join the scary, cool Axe Gang, and willing

00:09:40.190 --> 00:09:42.860
to engage in criminal behavior to do so.

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:46.520
Problem is, he picks on the wrong apartment
community, and Sing's ability to fight is

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:50.540
severely tested by some outrageously awesome
characters.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:51.540
First Blood

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:54.980
Who would have thought that Sylvester Stallone
could make a tragic, thought-provoking movie

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.990
about the dangers of violence and how war
destroys a man?

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:02.230
This psychologically and physically realistic
action movie centers on a man a decade removed

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:04.850
from the Vietnam War, but still fighting it.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:08.570
After a mental break in Washington, it's up
to John Rambo's old commanding officer to

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:12.520
save the on-the-run ex-soldier from himself
and authorities.

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:14.459
The Purge: Election Year

00:10:14.459 --> 00:10:18.640
The Purge movies have gotten a surprising
amount of mileage out of an implausible premise.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:22.620
In the near future, crime has been almost
completely eliminated in the U.S. thanks to

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:26.390
occasional "purges"—set periods of time
in which violence is permissible, allowing

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.070
people to get all their bad impulses out of
their systems.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:33.380
The third film in the series, The Purge: Election
Year, imagines the political and electoral

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.680
implications for a country that "purges."

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:39.720
Elizabeth Mitchell plays Senator Charlie Roan,
the sole survivor of a "Purge Night" family

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:43.070
massacre, who's running for president on a
promise to end purges.

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:48.029
Of course, she has to survive even more sinister
behavior and coordinated attacks by her political

00:10:48.029 --> 00:10:51.779
opposition in her attempt to find safety,
and then she has to win the election on top

00:10:51.779 --> 00:10:54.529
of that, so the odds are stacked against her.

00:10:54.529 --> 00:10:55.750
The Equalizer

00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:00.380
Technically speaking, The Equalizer is a remake
of a vaguely remembered action TV series from

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:01.380
the '80s.

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:04.680
But it's such an elegantly-made, fast-paced
flick that it's hard to fathom that it began

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.769
life as a cheesy CBS show.

00:11:06.769 --> 00:11:11.079
The spry and charismatic Denzel Washington
stars as Robert McCall, an ex-government man

00:11:11.079 --> 00:11:14.720
trying to balance out the horrible things
he did by now helping people who really need

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.329
his unique set of skills.

00:11:16.329 --> 00:11:20.230
This time, it's McCall against some truly
frightening Russian mobsters, and, as the

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:24.460
title indicates, he has an uncanny ability
to even out the playing field no matter who's

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:25.720
standing against him.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:26.720
Thanks for watching!

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.041
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:11:29.041 --> 00:11:31.470
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

